Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• `event_name`: filter the install event (`'first_open'`) and the uninstall event (`'app_remove'`).  
• `event_timestamp`: micro‑seconds since epoch – lets us calculate the “within 7 days” window (7 days = 604 800 000 000 µs).  
• `user_pseudo_id`: stable Firebase user identifier – used to group events that belong to the same user.  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX` (pseudo‑column that appears when you query the wildcard `events_*` tables): restricts the scan to August–September 2018 (`BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'`).  

Typical filter / join conditions that will be needed  

1. `_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'`  
2. `event_name = 'first_open'` or `event_name = 'app_remove'`  
3. `app_remove.event_timestamp   <= first_open.event_timestamp + 604800000000`  → uninstall within 7 days  
4. `app_remove.event_timestamp  >= first_open.event_timestamp`              → any uninstall after install  
5. users that satisfy (uninstall within 7 days) are separated from users that never satisfy (any uninstall after install).  

Below are ten exploratory → analytic queries that culminate in the percentage you asked for.  
Every query is capped with `LIMIT 20` so you can run them one‑by‑one and inspect sample rows/results.

```sql
-- 1. Description: list every distinct event name that appears during Aug–Sep 2018.
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: look at a few uninstall events (event_name = 'app_remove').
SELECT
  _TABLE_SUFFIX AS event_date,
  user_pseudo_id,
  event_timestamp
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  AND event_name = 'app_remove'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: look at a few install events (event_name = 'first_open').
SELECT
  _TABLE_SUFFIX AS event_date,
  user_pseudo_id,
  event_timestamp
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  AND event_name = 'first_open'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: first install time per user during Aug–Sep 2018.
SELECT
  user_pseudo_id,
  MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  AND event_name = 'first_open'
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: join installs with uninstalls to see uninstall events within 7 days.
WITH first_open AS (
  SELECT
    user_pseudo_id,
    MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
), uninstall AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, event_timestamp AS remove_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'app_remove'
)
SELECT
  f.user_pseudo_id,
  f.first_open_ts,
  u.remove_ts
FROM first_open f
JOIN uninstall u
  ON f.user_pseudo_id = u.user_pseudo_id
 WHERE u.remove_ts <= f.first_open_ts + 604800000000   -- 7 days
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: users that uninstalled within 7 days of install.
WITH first_open AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
), uninstall AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_remove_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'app_remove'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT
  f.user_pseudo_id,
  f.first_open_ts,
  u.first_remove_ts
FROM first_open f
JOIN uninstall u
  ON f.user_pseudo_id = u.user_pseudo_id
WHERE u.first_remove_ts <= f.first_open_ts + 604800000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: users that ever uninstalled (after the install), regardless of 7 days.
WITH first_open AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
), uninstall AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_remove_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'app_remove'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT
  f.user_pseudo_id,
  f.first_open_ts,
  u.first_remove_ts
FROM first_open f
JOIN uninstall u
  ON f.user_pseudo_id = u.user_pseudo_id
WHERE u.first_remove_ts >= f.first_open_ts
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: total number of users who installed during Aug–Sep 2018.
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id) AS total_installed_users
FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
  AND event_name = 'first_open'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: count users that either
-- (a) never uninstalled, or
-- (b) uninstalled but not within 7 days.
WITH first_open AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
), uninstall AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_remove_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'app_remove'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS users_retained_or_late_uninstall
FROM first_open f
LEFT JOIN uninstall u
  ON f.user_pseudo_id = u.user_pseudo_id
WHERE u.first_remove_ts IS NULL                       -- never uninstalled
   OR u.first_remove_ts > f.first_open_ts + 604800000000  -- uninstalled after 7 days
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: final percentage of users that
-- did NOT uninstall within 7 days (i.e., they either never uninstalled or did so after 7 days).
WITH first_open AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_open_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'first_open'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
), uninstall AS (
  SELECT user_pseudo_id, MIN(event_timestamp) AS first_remove_ts
  FROM `firebase-public-project.analytics_153293282.events_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180801' AND '20180930'
    AND event_name = 'app_remove'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
), stats AS (
  SELECT
    COUNT(DISTINCT f.user_pseudo_id)                                  AS total_installs,
    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE
                     WHEN u.first_remove_ts IS NULL
                       OR u.first_remove_ts > f.first_open_ts + 604800000000
                     THEN f.user_pseudo_id
                   END)                                               AS kept_or_late_uninstall
  FROM first_open f
  LEFT JOIN uninstall u
    ON f.user_pseudo_id = u.user_pseudo_id
)
SELECT
  kept_or_late_uninstall / total_installs * 100 AS pct_kept_or_late_uninstall
FROM stats
LIMIT 20;
```

Run the queries in order; the last one (`Query 10`) yields the requested percentage of users that did not uninstall within seven days (or never uninstalled) among all users who installed in August and September 2018.
